thank you very much yes we as you know  we are hosting the asia-europe meeting  as I'm here in Brussels this week  and in light of this I'm very happy that  the Commission just a couple of hours  ago adopted the EU Vietnam trade and  investment agreements so both of these  agreements showing our strong commitment  to our partnership with Vietnam these  agreements are important for many  reasons of course they will help as our  trade policy does to increase trade and  investment growth jobs boosting trade  with one of Asia's most dynamic  economies European companies will get  preferential access to the growing and  quickly developing markets obvious now  with more than 92 million consumers and  Vietnam exporters will get easier access  to Europe for their products this will  help also to spread our standards and  create better possibilities for  effecting change when it comes to human  rights and the protection of citizens  the trade agreement will remove 99% of  our tariffs opening up fantastic  possibilities for our companies and our  farmers to export more to Vietnam  exporting will be easier Vietnam is  bringing their standards in line with  ours which are international standards  and traditional European products will  be protected from imitation 169 food and  drink specialities geographical  indication such as Roquefort  Rioja wine prosciutto de Parma etc are  protected investment will become easier  and safer access to public procurement  services etc the trade agreement  includes strong rules of state-owned  enterprises and state subsidies will  which will help create a better level  playing field so there will be a better  legal certainty and adequate level of  protection for our investors Vietnam  also goes as all our trade agreements  nowadays beyond commercial  considerations containing ambitious  provisions or sustainable development a  firm commitment on both sides to  implement the conventions of the ILO the  International Labor Organization and I'm  